 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508084,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You  are going to bake cookies, using the same recipe as above. You find out that you have 27 cups of flour in your pantry. Assuming you have all the other ingredients necessary, how many cookies can you make with 27 cups of flour?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Set up the two ratios as proportions.</p>\n<p>Let <i>x</i> = the number of cookies you can make.</p>\n<p>It helps many students to create a table to help set up their ratios.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Recipe</td>\n<td>What I have or want</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cups of flour</td>\n<td>2.25</td>\n<td>27</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cookies</td>\n<td>60</td>\n<td><i>x</i></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Set up your proportion.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{2.25}}{{60}} = \\frac{{27}}{x}\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2.25x = \\left( {60} \\right)\\left( {27} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Cross multiply.200x</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2.25x = 1,620\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\frac{{2.25x}}{{2.25}} = \\frac{{1,620}}{{2.25}}\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"x = 720\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>You can make 720 cookies.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "720 cookies"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
